Z||000000||swoods||08-07-2001||03:33 AM||||How hard is it to convert an automatic to a manual 4 speed.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Capt Fiero||08-07-2001||09:14 AM||||Some people claim to have done it in a weekend and I dont see how they did it without being superman or superwoman, as you have to remove most of the interior, drop the steering coloumb, remove the auto tranny cooler lines and put the clutch hyd lines in there place, do a couple of quick wiring mods to get around the fact that the auto has a neutral start safty switch on the columb and the standard is designed to have it on the clutch pedal.  Then there is dropping the cradle to pull the auto out and swapping flywheels and instlalling a clutch and putting the standard trans in its place then putting it all back up in there with your new slave cylnder.  You can see tons of pics on my web page.  I dont have specific swap pics but you can see just how much had to be taken apart to do the swap.  My web page is <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/capt_fiero2000/capts_page.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/capt_fiero2000/capts_page.html</A>  <BR> <BR>the page is more centerd around my engine build than anything else.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Capt Fiero||08-07-2001||09:51 AM||||I forgot to mention, if you are on a high speed connection and car recieve large emails, I can email or ICQ File Transfer you a bunch of pics of my swap.  I will look into setting up a downloadable link if enough people ask for the pics. All of my build and transfer pics should be under 5 meg.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Capt Fiero||08-07-2001||10:42 AM||||Ok something went wrong and my pages are dead. I will try and get them back up soon. But I still have the zip file 3 meg in size if you want it.<BR>[This message has been edited by Capt Fiero (edited 08-07-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Capt Fiero (edited 08-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||fix||08-07-2001||10:29 PM||||I'm half way through this swap myself.  I bought 2 fieros a while back.  One was an auto with a bad engine but everything else was fine and the other was a 5 speed with a good engine but the front end was smashed.  I hate automatics anyway, so I figured I'd just swap the tranny too.  For me it's not that much work.  I'm going to use the entire wiring harness, computer, steering column, and anything else I need from the 5 speed car.  If I had to modify the wiring harness and steering column it would be much more difficult.<P>The worst part is if your car has cruise.  I don't have this problem, but if your car has cruise you have to put the switches down on the pedals so if you push the clutch in it doesn't continue to rev and just blow you're engine.  I'm not sure exactly what all this takes.  <P>My advice is not to do this swap unless you already have the parts readily available to you like I do.  It's expensive and time consuming and when you're done your car is no better than it came from the factory.<P>||||reg||1
